  "hints": [
    "State search can model all six operations, but reachable quantities also share a divisibility invariant.",
    "Every reachable amount is a multiple of gcd(x,y). The total cannot exceed x+y.",
    "Return target <= x+y and target % gcd(x,y) == 0.",
    "The Euclidean pouring process realizes multiples of the gcd within total capacity; the two conditions are necessary and sufficient."
  ],
  "editorial": "Filling and pouring produce amounts in the integer lattice generated by the capacities, whose step is gcd(x,y). The Euclidean pouring process realizes the needed multiples, while x+y bounds the combined storage. Check both conditions. For independent verification, the oracle uses breadth-first search over actual (left_volume,right_volume) states and all allowed operations.",
